Package: runix-audit-broker
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: privileged audit broker for the Runix durable-audit system
 A small, single-purpose, socket-activated daemon that appends a validated
 audit record to the root-owned Runix system sink on behalf of an
 unprivileged caller. The caller is identified by SO_PEERCRED (never by the
 payload); the broker performs no mutations and exposes a small set of request
 types (open_intent, write_outcome, emit, redeem_receipt, capabilities) over a
 local AF_UNIX socket, framed and parsed strictly.
 .
 It is the "strong" resolution of the Runix durable-audit authority matrix:
 the component that lets an unprivileged system-scope mutation obtain a
 system-durable audit record without granting it write access to the system
 sink or running privileged R.
